Thanks to @_akhaliq for sharing our work! We are excited to introduce GameWorld, a standardized and verifiable evaluation framework for multimodal game agents. It includes 34 browser games and 170 tasks, featuring 18 multimodal agent baselines that cover both computer-use agents with raw keyboard and mouse actions and generalist multimodal agents with semantic action parsing.

GameWorld demonstrates that even state-of-the-art agents still perform far below novice human players. Watch our live runs and check out the project page and GitHub for more details.

@_akhaliq: "GameWorld: Towards Standardized and Verifiable Evaluation of Multimodal Game Agents"

Thank you @_akhaliq for sharing our work on game agents! We see games as a natural testbed for multimodal agents, combining visual understanding, reasoning, planning, and action execution under clear rules and goals.

Many existing benchmarks focus on static states and final results, overlooking dynamics and process. With GameWorld, we hope to help push evaluation toward agents’ full interactive behavior over time.

