Just added this blog as a project page to help more people learn about state-of-the-art full-duplex voice models.

@bicro_ highlights Moshi as one of the best open-source full-duplex voice models. Its dense architecture prompted a few days of study and diagramming to understand it better.

The linked paper introduces Moshi, a speech-text foundation model and full-duplex spoken dialogue framework. Unlike traditional systems that rely on separate components like voice activity detection, speech recognition, dialogue management, and text-to-speech, Moshi aims to unify these into a more integrated approach.

🚀 Excited to see our work accepted by ECCV 2026.

